Package: iq
Type: Package
Title: Protein Quantification in Mass Spectrometry-Based Proteomics
Version: 2.2.0
Authors@R: c(person(c("Thang", "V."), "Pham", email = "t.pham@amsterdamumc.nl",
                    role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
                    comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-0333-2492")),
             person(c("Alex", "A."), "Henneman",
                    role = c("ctb"),
                    comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-3746-4410")))
Maintainer: Thang V. Pham <t.pham@amsterdamumc.nl>
Description: An implementation of the MaxLFQ algorithm by
    Cox et al. (2014) <doi:10.1074/mcp.M113.031591> using least-squares analysis in a comprehensive
    pipeline for processing proteomics data in data-independent acquisition mode
    (Pham et al. 2020 <doi:10.1093/bioinformatics/btz961>, and a new algorithm using the conjugate gradient method
    Pham et al. 2026 <doi:10.1021/acs.jproteome.5c01038>).
    It offers additional options for protein quantification using
    the N most intense fragment ions, using all fragment ions, 
    the median polish algorithm by Tukey (1977, ISBN:0201076160), 
    a robust linear model, and fragment weighting. A new 'iq' format enables the processing of large-scale datasets.
    In general, the tool can be used to integrate
    multiple proportional observations into a single quantitative value.
Depends: R (>= 4.0.0)
